<title>USA: Timberland ends kids clothing pact.</title>
<headline>Timberland ends kids clothing pact.</headline>
<dateline>TRATHAM, N.H. 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Apparel and footwear maker The Timberland Co and Lollytogs Ltd said on Wednesday that they have mutually agreed to end their licensing arrangement.</p>
<p>Lollytogs had been the licensee for a line of Timberland children's clothing, the companies said in a joint statement.</p>
<p>Lollytogs, a privately held company headquartered in New York, is the maker of children's wear.</p>
</text>
